Inclusion criteria:
1. Patient 18-60 years of age;
2. Patient clinically stabilized, for at least 6 months, as defined by a)	low intensity of positive symptoms, i.e. PANSS P1, P2 and P3 items < 4.
3. Patient treated with oral antipsychotics (in mono or polytherapy, with second- or first-generation antipsychotics);
4. Patients with a PSP score >70 at baseline
5. Patient affiliated to health insurance (beneficiary or beneficiary’s family);
6. Patient informed of the results of the preliminary medical examination;
7. Patient able to understand the aims and risks of the research (assisted by his/her curator, if applicable (if subject under curatorship*))*Subjects under limited guardianship (i.e. French “curatelle”) can participate to the study.
8. Informed consent signed by patient (with assistance of  his/her curator, if applicable    (if subject under curatorship*))
9. Patient with a diagnosis of schizophrenia spectrum disorder (SSD): schizophrenia, schizophreniform, schizoaffective disorder or brief psychotic episode according to DSM-5;
10. Patient with: a)	Either a cycloid psychosis (CP) phenotype according to By-CP (score >=80%; Lozère, 2024) b)	Or another (non-CP) psychotic phenotype;  (By-CP score < 80%)
11. Outpatient followed by an ambulatory psychiatrist;
12. Patient with an identified caregiver
Exclusion criteria:
1. Patient hospitalized in a psychiatric ward;
2. Patient in an exclusion period defined by another research protocol;
3. Patient under guardianship (i.e. French ‘tutelle’);
4. Patient with care under constraint
5. Patients deprived of freedom because of a judicial measure.
6. Inability to give the patient the written consent form (emergency situation)
7. Patient with a recent psychotic episode (during the last 6 months);
8. Patient treated with long-acting injection of antipsychotics (due to feasibility constraints and to the fact that these treatments remain essentially proposed to non-compliant patients with high risk of acute cessation and loss to follow-up);
9. Patient treated with clozapine (in mono or polytherapy – highly resistant patients, specificities of the relapses under clozapine (Luykx et al., 2020));
10. Patient considered by his psychiatrists to be at serious risk of harm to self or others (e.g. previous aggressive or suicidal behaviors);
11. Neurological or severe medical condition other than psychosis;
12. Pregnancy (verified by urinary test at enrollment for women of childbearing age);
13. Current breastfeeding;
14. Patient involved in another Investigational Medicinal Product trial;
